nce the race was expected to come down to the two Americans, " [:a {:href "/athletes/51511"} "Mike O’Brien"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/51316"} "George DiCarlo"] ". By 200 metres of the final they had pulled away from the pack. But DiCarlo found the water warmer than he liked and fell off the pace by 800 metres, leaving O’Brien in control. He would eventually win gold in 15:05.20, but DiCarlo did hang on for the silver medal, followed by West German " [:a {:href "/athletes/47890"} "Stefan Pfeiffer"] " in third. A few weeks later Salnikov won the Friendship Games 1,500 in 15:03.51. O’Brien commented after his win, “Obviously 15:05 is a long way from 14:54. I think, though, that if he’d have been in the same pool swimming right next to me, I could’ve given him a good race.” It’s nice to think so."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "478"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51511"} "Mike O'Brien"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "15:21.04 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "15:05.20 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "456"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51316"} "George DiCarlo"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "15:22.88 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "15:10.59 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47890"} "Stefan Pfeiffer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"}